Subject: [PATCH] sensor: ina219: power down on PM suspend

PM_DEVICE_ACTION_SUSPEND wrote INA219_MODE_SLEEP (0b100, "ADC off") to the
configuration register. The datasheet specifies the low supply current only
for power-down mode (0b000): 6 uA typ / 15 uA max, against 0.7 mA typ / 1 mA
max otherwise. Suspend now writes INA219_MODE_OFF, the same as TURN_OFF.

Resume already runs ina219_init(), which resets the part and rewrites the
configuration and calibration registers, so nothing is lost across suspend.

diff --git a/drivers/sensor/ti/ina219/ina219.c b/drivers/sensor/ti/ina219/ina219.c
index 9d88e60dc..2ee3da40e 100644
--- a/drivers/sensor/ti/ina219/ina219.c
+++ b/drivers/sensor/ti/ina219/ina219.c
@@ -234,7 +234,7 @@ static int ina219_pm_action(const struct device *dev,
 	case PM_DEVICE_ACTION_RESUME:
 		return ina219_init(dev);
 	case PM_DEVICE_ACTION_SUSPEND:
-		reg_val = INA219_MODE_SLEEP;
+		reg_val = INA219_MODE_OFF;
 		break;
 	case PM_DEVICE_ACTION_TURN_OFF:
 		reg_val = INA219_MODE_OFF;
